> Things you will/might need to change:
> SCSI card: Suggest DEC QLogic KZPBA-CA

Good card, good choice, other options are the KZPAA (Narrow) and KZPCA (U2
LVD), both will work in a PWS.

> SCSI CDRom: Suggest DEC Toshiba XM6201B or DEC RRD43 or higher ***

Plextor is another good choice.  

> Video Card: DEC 4D10T, 3D30, 4D20, Elsa Gloria Synergy 8mb, Diamond Fire 
> Pro 100, Permedia 2 8mb or compatible, PCI only.

Will the S3 cards work in a PWS?  They'll provide a cheap 8-bit card, and it
used to be possible to use some non-DEC versions of the cards.  

    PB2GA-JA (S3 Trio64 2MB)
    PB2GA-JB (S3 Trio64 1MB)
    PB2GA-JC (S3 Trio64V+ 1MB)
    PB2GA-JD (S3 Trio64V+ 2MB)

The cheapest way to get 24-bit colour (or run DECwindows period, for that
matter) is likely to be to retarget the display to another system running
X-Windows.  I ran a PWS 433au for about 7 years, and only a few months of
that time was with a Elsa Gloria Synergy (don't waste your money on one of
these they're trash).

> Hard Disk: Seagate or DEC branded Quantum 4gb to 36gb SCSI2 fast

Running a modern version of VMS you should be able to use just about any
SCSI HD.

> NIC: DEC DE450 or DE500

Why?  It already has a built in NIC.

> RAM: PC66-100 ECC CL2 256mb (max per stick)in matched pairs.

FYI, I found that my PWS did not like PC133 DIMMs.

> 4mb L3 Cache module: not absolutely necessary, but nice to have.

2mb L3 seems easier to obtain.  Question, is the L3 Cache a requirement?  I
don't see why it should be, but someone yesterday indicated that it is.

